<description>&lt;p&gt;The Indigenous Guard has taken up arms against President De la Espriella after a fifth bombing killed nine ELN members and a separate army bombing killed eight ELN fighters in the southwest. A car bomb at Casanare toll booths injured four women and a drone strike on a police station wounded six officers, while a drone attack in Guapi, Cauca killed one Marine and wounded four soldiers. Colombia supports international initiatives against organized crime and has reappointed Viviane Morales to De la Espriella’s government, while the extradition of Mocho Olmedo, head of Front 33, to the United States was executed. There were 225 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMihgFBVV95cUxPZlNzNUVOUHAyRWszSFZIUVd3cnhSalNPVGFIRUZhYUc1c1JldTRFYWRJSy05Z0ZEeEk0MjlxZ0o3Z3FVRTRtTnB5dzl5VE1NTXpUY2FVajRsRTJCOWpnZ052SXczN1E4c0JRZS1lcmZCR3hydXpJSEFqTjlqSkp0bTVqcXc1UQ?oc=5&quot;&gt;ReliefWeb&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiggFBVV95cUxOY3k4cHo0TV9FUUFleHZFQUVHTkZZUDZ5STZqbm1VMW1kdlRtcVI3bjlvcjVTWVlKblo4N1JlTlNuTXlBWjVNWUV3eHM3ejc3c2xERzFadnFFRFBLbnZvWUxXNy15TVkta25ONTVzaHp3N2hhTHdld2x3bFVtUWNiZjd3?oc=5&quot;&gt;ReliefWeb&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMivAFBVV95cUxOOEdwdnRKbjNCNlk0U0ZTSUJFYkNBSkJ0RG1adnVfbGxsNjc1R1FPV3loUVhYemVGLXVJVlBEejdxQ1FHdnZNRldwWkFKMDdPTTVSZlhJS19kZVBQZ01ldkhWbkZqdUZoV2RncVNfaEQzLUpfd05yX3VWbkktbllSSk4ycUJOd2JoUGlFcnk4aURsVnJWUHU4SVNyb193MktFV3ZfdUJobksxRnp1blJEVlpWblFEbWZrc1V2dg?oc=5&quot;&gt;ColombiaOne.com&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMixgFBVV95cUxNN0YwaDlOaGZEMTdpanQtZzBKMzJjY2Q3ZGpsM1lNLVpCVWZzODFxazNtYUYzOC1Qb2VXTXZld0QyZ1k0alBsc2l2Wk1ZbDlCbmdvWlc2enpmZ3dpV2VDTTZIOGZpZkpwYVJQcHEyY044QmNNVDROQ1k2cEY4UVpLY3RJUVRUY2VGS3BpR3BxNTZPQ